WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.797
This retention example begins with the recent activity view.

00:00:03.797 --> 00:00:09.497
The first common table expression finds the most recent transaction for each customer.

00:00:09.497 --> 00:00:13.447
The next stage applies a sixty day inactivity rule.

00:00:13.447 --> 00:00:16.897
Why keep that threshold outside the shared view?

00:00:16.897 --> 00:00:20.442
Because another report may want ninety days instead.

00:00:20.442 --> 00:00:24.392
The view owns the stable definition of recent activity.

00:00:24.392 --> 00:00:27.218
The report owns the temporary business rule.
